# Icons: always Iconify

All icons must come from [Iconify](https://iconify.design) through our shared `Icon` wrapper. Do not use inline SVG icons, emoji-as-icons, lucide-svelte, or other icon libraries.

## Patterns

- Import `Icon` from `#lib/components/ui/icon/index.js`.
- Pass an Iconify id: `prefix:name` (e.g. `lucide:star`, `selfhst:imdb`).
- Style with Tailwind on `class` (`size-4`, `text-rating`, brand colors, etc.).
- Register new icon sets in [`src/lib/icons.ts`](src/lib/icons.ts) via `@iconify-json/<set>` + `addCollection` before using them.

```svelte
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<script lang="ts">
	import { Icon } from '#lib/components/ui/icon/index.js';
</script>

<Icon icon="lucide:play" class="size-3.5 shrink-0" />
<a href={imdbHref} aria-label="View on IMDb">
	<Icon icon="selfhst:imdb" class="h-4 w-auto" />
</a>
```

```svelte
<!-- ❌ BAD — inline SVG / other icon packages -->
<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24">…</svg>
```

## Do not

- Hand-roll icon SVGs in components
- Import icons from `lucide-svelte`, `svelte-icons`, etc.
- Use Iconify ids whose collection is not registered in `icons.ts`
